  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Hebrew translation of values/strings.xml.

  Placeholders are POSITIONAL (%1$s / %1$d) and keep their numbers.
  Apostrophes and quotation marks are written RAW: Compose Multiplatform only
  unescapes \uXXXX, \n, \t and \\, so a backslash would reach the UI.
  "LatentJam" and "SMART" are names and stay untranslated, in Latin script.
  No bidi control characters here: the framework mirrors the layout. Compose
  picks a paragraph's direction from its first strong character, so a
  sentence never OPENS with a Latin name (that would lay it out left to right).
  Actions are verbal nouns (הפעלה, מחיקה) and instructions are impersonal
  (אפשר ל…, הקשה ל…): the UI stays gender-neutral.
  Hebrew distinguishes one / two / other (CLDR 42+); every plural carries all
  three and keeps its numeral, so the noun can agree with it.
-->
